- Put the destination of a forwarded receive in its invoice
  `StartLightningReceive` takes `hint_address`, the Ark address to put in the
  route hints of the invoice instead of the address of the claim key. A wallet
  that forwards a receive can then let users of the server pay the destination
  directly. An arkoor that pays the invoice must pay that address, and in
  expiry payout mode bind the output to its mailbox.
- Report the delivery of an invoice paid by arkoor in expiry payout mode
  A receive paid by arkoor settles when the server co-signs the arkoor, before
  the payer registers it and posts it to the receiver. The server now records
  the outputs at co-sign and marks each one delivered once it is registered
  and posted to the mailbox of the address in the invoice.
  `CheckLightningReceive` reports it in `delivered`. The migration adds the
  table `arkoor_receive_output`.
